/* An original, server-rendered reference guide. The calculations and source notes are educational. */
const categories=[
 {name:'Cash, current accounts and savings',typical:'Usually included',detail:'Money you own, whether kept in cash or in qualifying accounts. Do not count the same money twice when moving it between accounts.'},
 {name:'Gold and silver',typical:'Depends on applicable rules',detail:'Use a suitable valuation date and purity. Schools differ on personal jewellery, so include only what follows the guidance you use.'},
 {name:'Shares, funds and other investments',typical:'Requires assessment',detail:'Investment intention, ownership and the underlying assets can affect how much is zakatable. Enter only the qualifying value.'},
 {name:'Trading stock and business inventory',typical:'Often included when held for sale',detail:'Assess qualifying stock and trade receivables under the approach that applies to the business. Do not treat all equipment as resale stock.'},
 {name:'Money owed to you',typical:'Depends on recoverability',detail:'A debt that is likely to be collected may be treated differently from a disputed or uncollectable amount.'},
 {name:'Home, clothes and personal car',typical:'Generally excluded for personal use',detail:'Ordinary personal-use items are generally treated differently from similar goods acquired to resell.'},
 {name:'Pensions and retirement accounts',typical:'Needs case-specific guidance',detail:'Access, ownership, pension type and scholarly school can affect the assessment. An entire headline pot is not automatically equivalent to cash.'},
 {name:'Loans and other liabilities',typical:'Some may be deductible',detail:'Only include amounts your chosen religious guidance allows. A whole future mortgage or years of bills should not be deducted automatically.'}
];
const steps=[
 {title:'Choose the assessment date',text:'Identify the date used to review your wealth and check whether a lunar year (hawl) is relevant. If you are uncertain when your Zakat year began, get qualified guidance rather than assuming that the previous Ramadan is your personal anniversary.'},
 {title:'List qualifying assets',text:'Add cash, savings, gold and silver, relevant trade stock and investment values. Enter only the part you have determined is zakatable. Avoid counting one asset in two categories.'},
 {title:'Apply the appropriate liabilities',text:'Review payments you actually owe and which liabilities are deductible in your circumstances. Be careful with the entire balance of long-term loans and ongoing living costs.'},
 {title:'Check the Nisab benchmark',text:'Enter verified gold and silver prices for the same day and currency. Select the gold or silver reference according to guidance you follow; either benchmark can produce a different eligibility threshold.'},
 {title:'Calculate the conditional amount',text:'Subtract qualifying liabilities from qualifying assets, compare the result with the selected Nisab, and calculate 2.5% of net qualifying wealth where the conditions are met.'},
 {title:'Verify before paying',text:'Confirm hawl, asset treatments and eligibility with trusted religious guidance, then direct Zakat to eligible recipients or a suitable charitable organisation.'}
];
---
<section class="zakat-knowledge" aria-labelledby="zakat-knowledge-title" id="zakat-knowledge">
 <header>
  <h2 id="zakat-knowledge-title">How to calculate Zakat on savings, gold and other wealth</h2>
  <p>Zakat al-Mal is an obligation associated with qualifying wealth. A useful calculation begins by understanding the minimum threshold (<em>Nisab</em>), the relevant lunar year (<em>hawl</em>) and which assets and liabilities belong in the assessment. The calculator above handles the arithmetic; this guide explains the decisions you must make before trusting an estimate.</p>
 </header>
